{%- comment -%}
  Bassface Contact page — the board is `Sll8J`, 1440 only.

  A DOCUMENT PAGE with one form on it: no imagery, no map, no cards. Three
  numbered sections — `01 SEND A MESSAGE` beside `02 REACH US`, then
  `03 BEFORE YOU WRITE` across the full width — and that is the whole
  composition.

  ASSIGNED BY HAND. `templates/page.contact.json` exists but Shopify does not
  route a page to it automatically — the "contact" template has to be picked on
  the page itself in the admin, under Online Store > Pages > Contact > Theme
  template. That template is Dawn's own `page.contact.json`, overwritten: this
  section replaces both `main-page` and the stock `contact-form` section that
  used to be in it.

  EVERYTHING A MERCHANT MIGHT CHANGE IS A BLOCK, NOT A HARDCODED LINE. The three
  reach-us rows, the four social links and the four `BEFORE YOU WRITE` figures
  are all block types, so an address, a handle or a returns window changes in the
  theme editor rather than in a deploy. Shopify keeps blocks in ONE flat ordered
  list, so each run filters the list by type and renders its own; reordering a
  `social` past a `detail` in the editor changes nothing, since the two never
  share a container.

  THE FORM POSTS TO SHOPIFY, NOT TO US. `{% form 'contact' %}` renders the
  action, the authenticity token and the redirect back; there is no endpoint to
  configure and no JavaScript on this page beyond the shared entrance script.
  Submissions arrive at the sender email under Settings > Notifications.

  FIELD NAMES ARE THE CANONICAL FOUR, which is a deliberate departure from
  Dawn's stock `sections/contact-form.liquid`. Dawn posts the name, phone and
  comment under TRANSLATED keys — `contact[Comment]` and so on — so that the
  notification email reads in the merchant's language. The cost is that
  `form.body`, `form.name` and `form.phone` then come back empty when Shopify
  redirects after a validation failure, and the visitor loses everything they
  typed because the only field that ever fails is the email. Posting
  `contact[name]`, `contact[email]`, `contact[phone]` and `contact[body]` keeps
  all four values through a failed post, and those are the keys Shopify's own
  notification template already understands.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'bf-breadcrumb.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-reveal.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{{ 'bf-main-contact.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'bf-reveal.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{%- liquid
  assign details = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'detail'
  assign socials = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'social'
  assign facts = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'fact'
  assign form_id = 'ContactForm-' | append: section.id
-%}

<div class="main-contact">
  {%- comment -%}
    The crumb is the PAGE's title, not the section's heading, so the trail
    follows whatever the merchant renamed the page to — which is the thing a
    visitor navigating back up is looking for. Falls back to the heading if this
    template is ever rendered somewhere there is no page object.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%-
    render 'bf-breadcrumb',
    current: page.title | default: section.settings.heading,
    home_label: section.settings.breadcrumb_home,
    label: section.settings.breadcrumb_label
  -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    The entrance is the About page's and the product page's — <bf-reveal
    class="reveal reveal--rise"> clips a wrapper and climbs its single child out
    from under the top edge. It waits on the preloader handing over AND on
    reaching the viewport, so nothing plays behind a curtain that has not lifted.

    THE RESTING STATE IS THE VISIBLE ONE. Nothing is hidden until bf-reveal.js
    adds `is-concealed`, so a blocked script leaves a plain, usable form rather
    than a column of invisible fields.

    Anything holding a focusable control uses `main-contact__lift` instead of
    `reveal--rise` — same trigger, no clip, so focus rings survive. The note in
    bf-main-contact.css explains why that matters more here than anywhere else.

    --reveal-index is the stagger, one step per element within a group.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="main-contact__header">
    <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
      <h1 class="main-contact__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
    </bf-reveal>

    {%- if section.settings.description != blank -%}
      <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise" style="--reveal-index: 1">
        <p class="main-contact__intro">{{ section.settings.description }}</p>
      </bf-reveal>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="main-contact__main">
    {%- comment -%} 01 — SEND A MESSAGE {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="main-contact__column">
      {%- render 'bf-contact-head', number: '01', label: section.settings.form_label -%}

      {%- form 'contact', id: form_id, class: 'main-contact__form' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Shopify only ever rejects the email address on a contact form, but the
          errors object is iterated rather than tested for 'email' so a future
          field that can fail is reported instead of swallowed. `autofocus` with
          tabindex="-1" moves the visitor to the message on arrival, which is the
          only way they learn the post failed after a full page reload.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <div class="main-contact__status">
            <h3 class="main-contact__status-title" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{ section.settings.success_title }}
            </h3>
            <p class="main-contact__status-text">{{ section.settings.success_body }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- elsif form.errors -%}
          <div class="main-contact__status">
            <h3 class="main-contact__status-title" role="alert" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
              {{ 'templates.contact.form.error_heading' | t }}
            </h3>
            <ul class="main-contact__status-list" role="list">
              {%- for field in form.errors -%}
                <li>
                  {{ form.errors.translated_fields[field] | capitalize }}
                  {{ form.errors.messages[field] }}
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        <div class="main-contact__fields">
          <div class="main-contact__row">
            <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift">
              <div class="main-contact__field">
                <label class="main-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-name">
                  {{- section.settings.name_label -}}
                </label>
                <input
                  id="{{ form_id }}-name"
                  class="main-contact__input"
                  type="text"
                  name="contact[name]"
                  value="{% if form.name %}{{ form.name }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.name }}{% endif %}"
                  placeholder="{{ section.settings.name_placeholder | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="name"
                >
              </div>
            </bf-reveal>

            <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: 1">
              <div class="main-contact__field">
                <label class="main-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-email">
                  {{- section.settings.email_label -}}
                </label>
                <input
                  id="{{ form_id }}-email"
                  class="main-contact__input"
                  type="email"
                  name="contact[email]"
                  value="{% if form.email %}{{ form.email }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.email }}{% endif %}"
                  placeholder="{{ section.settings.email_placeholder | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  autocapitalize="off"
                  spellcheck="false"
                  aria-required="true"
                  {% if form.errors contains 'email' %}
                    aria-invalid="true"
                  {% endif %}
                  required
                >
              </div>
            </bf-reveal>
          </div>

          <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: 2">
            <div class="main-contact__field">
              <label class="main-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-phone">
                {{- section.settings.phone_label -}}
              </label>
              {%- comment -%}
                No `pattern` attribute. Dawn's is `[0-9\-]*`, which silently
                rejects the `+91` its own placeholder asks for — and the board's
                placeholder is `+91` too. A phone number that reaches the
                merchant slightly malformed is worth more than one the browser
                refused to send.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <input
                id="{{ form_id }}-phone"
                class="main-contact__input"
                type="tel"
                name="contact[phone]"
                value="{% if form.phone %}{{ form.phone }}{% elsif customer %}{{ customer.phone }}{% endif %}"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.phone_placeholder | escape }}"
                autocomplete="tel"
              >
            </div>
          </bf-reveal>

          <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: 3">
            <div class="main-contact__field">
              <label class="main-contact__label" for="{{ form_id }}-body">
                {{- section.settings.comment_label -}}
              </label>
              {%- comment -%}
                The closing tag sits hard against the output tag on purpose: a
                textarea renders every character between the tags, so newlines
                and indentation here would come back as leading whitespace in the
                field on a failed post.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <textarea
                id="{{ form_id }}-body"
                class="main-contact__input main-contact__input--area"
                name="contact[body]"
                rows="6"
                placeholder="{{ section.settings.comment_placeholder | escape }}"
              >{{ form.body }}</textarea>
            </div>
          </bf-reveal>

          <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: 4">
            <div class="main-contact__submit-wrap">
              <button class="main-contact__submit" type="submit">
                {{ section.settings.submit_label }}
              </button>
            </div>
          </bf-reveal>
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} 02 — REACH US {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="main-contact__column">
      {%- render 'bf-contact-head', number: '02', label: section.settings.reach_label -%}

      {%- if details.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="main-contact__details" role="list">
          {%- for block in details -%}
            <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: {{ forloop.index0 }}">
                <div class="main-contact__detail">
                  <span class="main-contact__detail-key">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>

                  {%- if block.settings.url != blank -%}
                    <a class="main-contact__detail-value main-contact__link" href="{{ block.settings.url }}">
                      {{- block.settings.value -}}
                    </a>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="main-contact__detail-value">{{ block.settings.value }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </bf-reveal>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if socials.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="main-contact__socials">
          {%- if section.settings.socials_label != blank -%}
            <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise">
              <p class="main-contact__socials-label">{{ section.settings.socials_label }}</p>
            </bf-reveal>
          {%- endif -%}

          <ul class="main-contact__socials-list" role="list">
            {%- for block in socials -%}
              <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <bf-reveal class="reveal main-contact__lift" style="--reveal-index: {{ forloop.index0 }}">
                  {%- comment -%}
                    16px against a 16px label, where the board draws 14. The
                    board's icon is an already-tightened path; ours is Lucide's
                    stroke glyph in a 24 viewBox where the ink only spans 6 to
                    18, so a 14px box would draw a 7px arrow. Same correction the
                    About page's CTA makes, and the same reason.

                    TWO ARROWS, AND THE FIRST ONE IS THE POINT. On hover the
                    label and its arrow shift right by an arrow's width while a
                    second arrow arrives from the left, and the link's own clip
                    is what makes the pair read as ONE arrow crossing the label
                    rather than two arrows appearing. This is the storefront's
                    primary-link gesture — Add to Bag, Checkout and the About
                    CTA already make it.

                    The lead arrow is aria-hidden and absolutely positioned, so
                    it adds nothing to the accessible name and nothing to the
                    link's width.

                    `rel` and `target` are the merchant's call, not ours: a
                    social link that steals the tab is a nuisance, so it opens in
                    a new one, and `noopener` is what stops that new tab reaching
                    back through window.opener.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <a
                    class="main-contact__social"
                    href="{{ block.settings.url | default: '#' }}"
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener"
                  >
                    <span class="main-contact__social-icon main-contact__social-icon--lead" aria-hidden="true">
                      {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: 16 -%}
                    </span>
                    <span class="main-contact__social-label">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                    <span class="main-contact__social-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                      {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: 16 -%}
                    </span>
                  </a>
                </bf-reveal>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} 03 — BEFORE YOU WRITE {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if facts.size > 0 -%}
    <section class="main-contact__block">
      {%- render 'bf-contact-head', number: '03', label: section.settings.facts_label -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        `role="list"` on every list in this section, and it is not belt and
        braces: Safari drops list semantics from any <ul> whose `list-style` is
        `none`, which is all three of them. The role puts the semantics back.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="main-contact__facts" role="list">
        {%- for block in facts -%}
          <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <bf-reveal class="reveal reveal--rise" style="--reveal-index: {{ forloop.index0 }}">
              <div class="main-contact__fact">
                <span class="main-contact__fact-key">{{ block.settings.label }}</span>
                <p class="main-contact__fact-value">{{ block.settings.value }}</p>
                <p class="main-contact__fact-desc">{{ block.settings.description }}</p>
              </div>
            </bf-reveal>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Contact page",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Page title",
      "default": "Contact"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "description",
      "label": "Intro paragraph",
      "default": "Order questions, sizing help, collabs, promos — or just say hi. We read everything and reply within two working days."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "breadcrumb_home",
      "label": "Breadcrumb home link",
      "default": "Home"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "breadcrumb_label",
      "label": "Breadcrumb landmark name",
      "info": "Read by screen readers to announce the navigation. Not shown.",
      "default": "Breadcrumb"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "01 — Send a message"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "form_label",
      "label": "Section label",
      "default": "SEND A MESSAGE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "name_label",
      "label": "Name field label",
      "default": "NAME"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "name_placeholder",
      "label": "Name field placeholder",
      "default": "Your name"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "email_label",
      "label": "Email field label",
      "info": "This is the only required field. Keep the asterisk.",
      "default": "EMAIL *"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "email_placeholder",
      "label": "Email field placeholder",
      "default": "you@email.com"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "phone_label",
      "label": "Phone field label",
      "default": "PHONE"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "phone_placeholder",
      "label": "Phone field placeholder",
      "default": "+91"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "comment_label",
      "label": "Message field label",
      "default": "COMMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "comment_placeholder",
      "label": "Message field placeholder",
      "default": "Tell us what's up — order number helps if it's about a delivery."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "submit_label",
      "label": "Submit button label",
      "default": "Submit"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "success_title",
      "label": "Success heading",
      "info": "Shown after the form is sent.",
      "default": "MESSAGE SENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "success_body",
      "label": "Success message",
      "default": "Thanks for writing in. We read everything and reply within two working days."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "02 — Reach us"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "reach_label",
      "label": "Section label",
      "default": "REACH US"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Email addresses and phone numbers come from the \"Contact detail\" blocks below."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "socials_label",
      "label": "Social links label",
      "info": "Leave blank to hide it.",
      "default": "FOLLOW"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "03 — Before you write"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "facts_label",
      "label": "Section label",
      "default": "BEFORE YOU WRITE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Figures come from the \"Fact\" blocks below. Four fit on one row at desktop."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "detail",
      "name": "Contact detail",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label",
          "default": "SUPPORT EMAIL"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Value",
          "default": "hello@bassface.in"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "url",
          "label": "Link",
          "info": "A mailto:, tel: or https: URL. Leave blank to render the value as plain text.",
          "default": "mailto:hello@bassface.in"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "social",
      "name": "Social link",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label",
          "default": "Instagram"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "url",
          "label": "URL"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "fact",
      "name": "Fact",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Label",
          "default": "PROCESSING"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "value",
          "label": "Figure",
          "info": "Kept short — this is set at 28px and sits on one line at desktop.",
          "default": "3–5 days"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "description",
          "label": "Description",
          "default": "Orders are packed and dispatched within three to five working days."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
